{
 "_about": "African states in order of independence, with UN admission dates. Built 2026-10-31 for c3 C3S104 (colonial blocks crack into countries, in this order) and C3S107 (one new GA dot per new African member).",
 "_sources": [
  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decolonisation_of_Africa — table \"African countries that have gained independence\" (Independence date), retrieved 2026-10-31",
  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_states_of_the_United_Nations — \"Date of admission\", retrieved 2026-10-31"
 ],
 "_notes": [
  "Ethiopia (never colonised; Italian occupation 1936-41) is not listed; it was a founding UN member (1945-11-13). Western Sahara (SADR) is excluded (not a UN member).",
  "Where Wikipedia lists several dates the main independence date is used (e.g. Cameroon 1960-01-01, Mauritania 1960-11-28, Namibia 1990-03-21, Zimbabwe 1980-04-18). Senegal and Mali became independent together as the Mali Federation (1960-06-20); Senegal left it on 1960-08-20.",
  "UN admission is the date of the successor state where names changed (Tanganyika 1961-12-14 -> United Republic of Tanzania). 1960 \"Year of Africa\": 17 African states became independent and 16 joined the UN that year (Nigeria Oct 7; the rest 20 Sep / 28 Sep)."
 ],
